<title>USA: Oak Technology to post $5 mln charge.</title>
<headline>Oak Technology to post $5 mln charge.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oak Technology Inc said Tuesday that it will post a $5 million charge after agreeing to a payment of a $5 million earnout in connection with its 1995 acquisition of Pixel Magic.</p>
<p>The earnout had been contingent upon Pixel Magic's achievement of certain performance criteria. The related charge is to be posted in the quarter ended June 30.</p>
<p>A wholly-owned subsidiary of Oak, Pixel Magic provides advanced image processing silicon and software technology.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
